# Agent Instructions

`{{ .name }}` is an Intropy transactional integration: a .NET 10 job that
sweeps its source port, queues each file on an internal topic, and runs each
queued file through a send pipeline that writes to its destination port.

## Project overview

- App id: `{{ .appId }}`
- Internal topic: `internal-{{ .appId }}` on the system's pub/sub. It is
  invisible to the system topology; the framework reads both names from
  `INTROPY_PUBSUB_NAME` / `INTROPY_TOPIC_NAME`, which the system host and the
  deployment set.
- Source port: `{{ .fromPort }}`; destination port: `{{ .toPort }}`. Both are
  declared in the system host's `Ports.cs`.
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .fromPort }}:Kind`, `Ports:{{ .toPort }}:Kind`: `Local` in
    Development; a deployment sets `Ports__<port>__Kind` (`Sftp`, `AzureBlob`)
{{- if not .empty }}
  - `PlatformServices:IdempotencyServiceAppId`: `{{ .idempotencyAppId }}`
  - `PlatformServices:BusinessIncidentServiceAppId`: `{{ .businessIncidentsAppId }}`
{{- end }}

## Important files

- `src/Configuration/Composition.cs`: DI registrations and
  `AddTransactionalIntegration`. The framework owns the receive side (sweep,
  publish, delete); there is no receive-side component code.
- `src/Configuration/Constants.cs`: component name, ports, context keys.
- `src/Send/`: the send pipeline steps and `SendRoute`, which composes them.
- `src/Model/`: the `In`, `Out` and `Line` records.
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Unit/`: step unit tests.
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: receive-side, send-pipeline and
  composition tests on `Intropy.Framework.Testing` fakes (fakes in `FakeEdges.cs`).
- `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dockerignore`: image build. The build context is
  the system folder: `docker build -f {{ .appId }}/Dockerfile -t {{ .appId }} .`

## Build and test

The job runs via its system host, which provides the storage bindings, the
pub/sub and the platform services.

```bash
task build
task test        # or task test:unit / task test:integration
task coverage    # Cobertura report under the integration project's TestResults/
```

## Development notes
{{ if .empty }}
- The step bodies throw `NotImplementedException`. Idempotency and business
  incidents are not wired; add `.WithIdempotency(...)` and
  `.WithBusinessIncidents(...)` in `src/Send/SendRoute.cs` and register their
  clients in `src/Configuration/Composition.cs`.
{{- else }}
- Idempotency keys off the order's `OrderId` / `OrderDate`.
- The `Sender` is a business step: a destination write failure routes a
  business incident instead of a broker retry.
{{- end }}

## Framework guidance

Framework how-to (pipelines, blocks, endpoints, Dapr components, testing) lives in the Intropy documentation at <https://docs.intropy.io>. For CLI facts, read `intropy template show` and `intropy <command> --help` at the moment you need them; template releases change.
